  -> every weak-* continuous datum moves by O(h); the floor jumps at h=0 only.
  -> 1_{G_0.2} is 0 for every h>0 and 1 at h=0 : discontinuous exactly at the ray endpoint.

=== SUMMARY (one-sidedness) ===
  max mass below eps  > 0  for all finite N   => 'floor >= eps' unprovable from finite data
  min mass below eps  = 0  for all finite N   => 'floor <  eps' unpinnable from finite data by itself
  both directions fail at every finite N; only the infinite datum (or a discontinuity) decides.
